Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  31 REMOVED_MONTH 01 ACCESSIONED ON  31 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 12 09 CLINICAL DATA  55 year old female with right ductal carcinoma in situ  Short stitch is superior  long stitch lateral  bowtie marks cephalad                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  A FEW SMALL SCATTERED FOCI OF MILDLY ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  MARGINS NEGATIVE  2  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH CALCIFICATIONS  3  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  4  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Diagnosis by  MELINDA J  FAN  MD Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 08 16                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 4cm oriented breast excision with a short stitch marking anterior  long stitch lateral  double stitches cephalad superior and a needle localization wire in place  The specimen is inked with superior and inferior aspect blue  anterior posterior black and medial lateral aspect green  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 1cm ill defined white dense fibrous scar which is abutting the posterior margin and less than 1mm from the closest lateral margin  There are areas of hemorrhage within and around the fibrous scar which corresponds to the tract of the needle localization wire  There is a small focal gritty area located adjacent to the scar that is 1 4cm from the closest posterior margin  No distinct masses are noted  The remainder of the breast parenchyma is unremarkable  Representative sectgions are taken as follows  Section Code  A  Scar with lateral posterior margin  B C  Scar with posterior margin  D  Scar with posterior lateral margin  E F  Scar with posterior margin with gritty area in cassette F  G  Scar with lateral margin  H I  Posterior margin  J  Lateral margin  K  Anterior margin  L  Inferior margin  Resident  PAULA ARNELL  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Kevin S  Hughes  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  06 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  06 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 13 22 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 1  REMOVED_DATE CM  95  EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN ALONG A BROAD FRONT  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  CRIBRIFORM TYPE  5   CONFINED TO THE REGION OF THE MASS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 11 21                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 03 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm yellow pink fatty tissue fragment Inked and sectioned to reveal a 1 0cm in greatest dimension ill defined  tan  firm lesion abutting multiple inked margins  A representative section is frozen as FX 1  now submitted in cassette A  The remainder of the lesion is submitted in cassettes B through D  The remainder of the specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes E through J  Resident  Jacqueline Haas  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   LEFT BREAST   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA APPROACHING THE INKED SURFACE  O R  Resident  STEPHEN LAU  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Horace C  Wu  MD O R  Consulting Pathologist s   Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Ashby Carter Moncure  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
