e breast at 12 o clock  This ill defined fibrous region is 1 8cm from the  anterior margin and 2 1cm from the posterior margin  A slightly firm   triangular white fibrous region is noted 2cm deeper to the ill defined fibrous  region along the anterior magin  0 3cm from the anterior margin and 5cm from  the deep margin  No clip is identified in either fibrous region  The region of  the anterior lower outer quadrant  an area with a previous biopsy and clip per  the clinical records  reveals white fibrous tissue with no mass or clip  identified  Lymph nodes are not detected in the lateral tissue     Additionally received in the same container is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm aggregate of  irregular yellow white fibroadipose tissue  which is serially sectioned to  reveal unremarkable yellow pink fatty cut surfaces  The following  representative sections are submitted      REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Hemorrhagic region in the inner middle breast with the region of the  clip and anterior margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and the posterior margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tissue intervening between the hemorrhagic cavity and the center portion of  the breast    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Ill defined fibrous region at 12 o clock  nearest anterior margin in   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Posterior margin adjacent to ill defined fibrous region    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tissue intervening between ill defined fibrous region and anterior lower  outer quadrant    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Anterior lower outer quadrant tissue    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Central tissue    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Slightly firm fibrous region  entirely submitted  closest anterior  margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tissue intervening between well and ill defined white fibrous regions    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Remainder of ill defined fibrous region    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional tissue from lower outer quadrant     C  Received fresh  labeled  left axillary node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm  aggregate of fibrofatty and lymph node tissue  which is dissected and palpated  to reveal tan lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm   The lymph nodes are tan pink  rubbery  and ovoid and are bisected to reveal  tan  homogeneous cut surfaces with regions of yellow adipose tissue replacement   The specimen is entirely submitted as follows      REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One lymph node  bisected  each cassette    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Intact lymph nodes    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Remaining fibroadipose tissue     D  Received fresh  labeled  left mastectomy skin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm  circular portion of skin excision  The skin is brown and unremarkable without  focal masses or lesions  The deep aspect of the specimen is surfaced by  lobular  yellow fibroadipose tissue  The specimen is serially sectioned to  reveal unremarkable brown to white pink cut surfaces and a representative  section is submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      E  Received fresh  labeled  right mastectomy skin   is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm  circular portion of skin  The skin is brown and unremarkable without focal  lesions  The deep aspect of the specimen is surfaced by unremarkable  yellow pink fibroadipose tissue  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal  unremarkable brown to white yellow cut surfaces and a representative section is  submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID          PART A  BREAST SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  RIGHT  PART B  BREAST SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  LEFT  PART C  LYMPH NODES DISSECTION  LEFT AXILLA  PART D  SKIN EXCISION  LEFT BREAST MASTECTOMY  PART E  SKIN EXCISION  RIGHT BREAST MASTECTOMY       report_end  , Unchecked.
