Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  CorrectedType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  ACCESSIONED ON  07 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 10 30 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided      REVISED REPORT     Reason for Revision  ADDITIONAL OUTSIDE MATERIAL RECEIVED Revised by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Revised on 21 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 11 45                                                                                     FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  C  90   AND INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  C  10    NOTE  The infiltrating carcinoma is in sections marked to correspond with the green and red pins  Intraductal carcinoma is multifocal and involves the green and red pin sections as well as sections corresponding to the white and yellow pins  Intraductal carcinoma focally extends virtually to an inked margin  No lymphatic or vascular invasion is identified  The pins were placed at the referring institution  Diagnosis by  Ben Zion Pilch  M D  Edited by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 07 13 Proofread by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 07 13                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTSIDE LOCATION REPORTS TO  W B Jerry Younger  M D  OUTSIDE INSTITUTION  HOSPITAL MT AUBURN OUTSIDE PATHOLOGIST  Linda Covell  M D  MOUNT AUBURN HOSPITAL DEPT OF PATH 330 MOUNT AUBURN STREET CAMBRIDGE  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID  OUTSIDE CLINICIAN  John Schuler  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Date of Procedure  18 JUN  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Slides  6 Blocks  0   report_end  , Unchecked.
