Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  19 MAY 97 ACCESSIONED ON  19 MAY 97 at 12 58 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  TUBULAR CARCINOMA  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE I  REMOVED_DATE CM  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU OCCUPYING FOUR OF EIGHT BLOCKS  HARBORING CALCIFICATIONS  AND FOCALLY EXTENDING TO ABOUT REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMOA IN SITU   RADIAL SCARS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The margin of the specimen appears free of the tumor  BREAST  LEFT   SPECIMEN  1  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA HARBORING CALCIFICATIONS  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA   RADIAL SCARS  FIBROSIS AND FOREIGN BODY GIANT CELL REACTION CONSISTENT WITH HEALED BIOPSY SITE  BREAST  LEFT   SPECIMEN  2  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  FEW SMALL FOCI  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA   Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 MAY 97 at 15 28                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 36 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm piece of firm white breast tissue that on cut sectioning reveals fibrosis  firm adipose tissue and small cysts  entirely submitted in A H  Labeled  1  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 3cm fragment of breast  inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm nodular area with microcysts  Entirely submitted in I N  with nodule in K N  Labeled  2  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm fragment of breast inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm nodular area  the rest is unremarkable  Representative sections are submitted from 0 W with nodules  area of microcalcification on mammogram  from P S  Resident  MARISA BALDASSANO  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  NO INFILTRATING CARCINOMA LARGE ENOUGH TO FREEZE  GROSS DIAGNOSES  2 AND  3  NO GROSS EVIDENCE OF INFILTRATING CARCINOMA O R  Resident  ESTHER OLIVA  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Lawrence R  Zukerberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION PART B  BR