result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 10 14 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast lump  short stitch superior  long stitch lateral  is a fragment of breast tissue measuring 6 x 6 x 1cm that is inked and sectioned to reveal a 1cm in largest diameter stellate  firm to gritty area in a lateral portion of the specimen  0 4cm from the closest margin  the posterior margin   Representative sections are submitted from lateral to medial in A through J  B through F contains the entire nodule   The specimen was over inked blue on the posterior margin and green over the superior margin  yellow over the inferior margin  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm aggregate of adipose tissue  Lymph node dissection is performed with lymph nodes submitted in cassettes K through Q  Resident  JUSTIN M  CATES  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS   RIGHT BREAST EXCISION   MARGINS FREE OF TUMOR  GROSS ONLY  O R  Resident  HONGMEI LI  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Robert Henry Young  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION PART B  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA    report_end  , Unchecked.
