Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  09 REMOVED_MONTH 03 ACCESSIONED ON  09 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 15 12 CLINICAL DATA  Invasive ductal carcinoma  left breast                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL   EXCISION  ONE LYMPH NODE FREE OF CARCINOMA   SEE NOTE   NOTE  Keratin positive tumor cells are not identified on three  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 Cam5 2 immunostained levels  BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEE TABLE 1   TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA Tumor size  Four nodules  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  see note   Grade  REMOVED_DATE Lymphatic vessel invasion  Not identified Blood vessel invasion  Not identified Margin of invasive carcinoma  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater for all nodules Location of ductal carcinoma in situ  Within the region of the masses Grade of ductal carcinoma in situ  2 Margin of ductal carcinoma in situ  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater Stains for receptors  Requested NOTE  The four masses are located in both the medial and lateral aspects of the breast and are physically separated by upwards of 6cm  Despite this significant distance between four masses  all four masses have a highly similar histomorphology appearance  This latter finding favors multifocal rather than multicentric disease  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 16 31                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block C   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  Breast  Left  block G   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  Breast  Left  block I   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  Breast  Left  block K   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 10 32 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary sentinel node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm irregular yellow rubbery lymph node which is bivalved and entirely submitted for frozen section as FX 1  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast stitch as 12   consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 4cm left simple mastectomy specimen with a stitch denoting the superior margin  There is a central overlying REMOVED_DATE x 3 3cm circular portion of skin which contains a 3 1cm nipple areolar complex which is grossly unremarkable  The margins of resection are marked with black inked  The specimen is serially sectioned at 5mm intervals from medial to lateral  Four distinct lesions are identified and are described below in a medial to lateral fashion  Lesion  1  most medial  measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE and extends 1 8cm of the deep margin and 1 7cm of the anterior superior margin  Lesion  2  medial  is located 1cm lateral to lesion  1 and is ill defined mass measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  The lesion extends to 3 5cm of the deep margin and 0 3cm of the anterior superior margin  Lesion  3  central  measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm and is located in the superior central portion of the breast and extends to 3 8cm of the deep margin to approximately 2cm of the anterior margin  The lesion is located approximately 6cm lateral to lesion  2  Lesion  2 3 have blue dye adjacent to them  Lesion  4 is  most lateral  measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm and is located 2 0cm from the deep margin and 4 3cm from the anterior margin  The 4th lesion is located approximately 4 5cm lateral to the largest lesion   lesion  3   The remainder of the tissue consists predominately of adipose tissue with a few foci of soft white fibrous tissue  Representative sections are submitted as follows  B D  Lesion  1  E G  Lesion  2  H I  Lesion  3  J  Shave margin  deep margin beneath lesion  3  K L  Lesion  4  M N  Sections of fibrous tissue between the different lesions  Gross Description by  TIM J  ROBINSON Resident  RANIA M  SELIEM  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLARY  BIOPSY   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  O R  Resident  MINDY J  HULL  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Ben Zion Pilch  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL   EXCISION PART B  BREAST LEFT  SIMPLE MASTECTOMY , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  10 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  10 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 09 37 CLINICAL DATA  Invasive carcinoma of the right breast and ductal carcinoma in situ in the left breast                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  MODERATE GRADE  PRESENT IN 1 OF 7 REPRESENTATIVE TISSUE BLOCKS  DISTANT FROM THE RESECTION MARGIN  SEE NOTE  ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  MULTIFOCAL  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEE NOTE  HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY WITH FOREIGN BODY GIANT CELL REACTION TO SUTURE  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 4 OF 4 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  NOTE  No stromal  blood vascular or lymphatic vessel invasion is identified  BREAST  RIGHT   MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE CARCINOMA  MULTIFOCAL  ASSOCIATED WITH AND AWAY FROM THE BIOPSY CAVITY   SEE NOTE  NOTE  All resection margins are free of invasive and in situ carcinoma  Invasive carcinoma forms 3 major masses  2 2cm  1 4cm and 1 0cm  Multiple smaller foci of invasive tumor associated with in situ carcinoma are also present  Invasive carcinoma is focally present 0 1cm from a deep resection margin  The invasive and in situ carcinomas display ductal and lobular features  The invasive ductal component is low grade  grade REMOVED_DATE No blood vascular or lymphatic vessel invasion is identified  IN SITU CARCINOMA  WITH DUCTAL AND LOBULAR FEATURES  EXTENSIVE  METASTATIC CARCINOMA PRESENT IN 2 OF 17 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES   SEE NOTE   NOTE  One of the lymph nodes contains more than 0 2cm of metastatic carcinoma distributed in the subcapsular sinus  Another lymph node contains scattered nests of tumor cells which are less than 0 2cm in agggregate  Positive keratin stains confirm these findings  SOFT TISSUE  ADDITIONAL RIGHT AXILLA   EXCISION  FIBROADIPOSE TISSUE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 16 22                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 45 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are three specimens  Labelled  left modified radical mastectomy   is a mastectomy specimen with a skin ellipse measuring REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm  On the skin ellipse there is also a 2 9cm long vertical well healed scar  The areola on the skin ellipse measures 2 9cm in diameter and has a nipple in the center with 1 2cm diameter  The specimen is oriented with a stitch designating the superior margin  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm biopsy cavity located below the well healed scar  The cavity is 0 5cm from the closest posterior resection margin  Around the biopsy cavity is relatively firm white yellow fibrous tissue  The inferior to the cavity there is a well circumscribed white 3 5cm in greatest diameter firm nodule  which is 0 2cm from the posterior  deep  margin  The remaining breast parenchyma appears grossly unremarkable  Representative sections are taken  Submitted in cassette A G  Section code  A  Biopsy cavity and nodule in relation to closest  deep  resection margin  B  Nodule C E  Biopsy cavity with adjacent nodule in relation to resection margin  F  Nodule G  Unremarkable breast parenchyma  representative section  In the axillary tail a suture designates the axillary nodes and in this area two lymph nodes are found  One lymph node measure 1 3cm in greatest diameter  the other 1 6cm in greatest diameter  The lymph nodes are submitted in cassettes H I  Additionally  two lymph nodes were also found in the axillary tail and are submitted in cassette J  Labelled  right modified radical mastectomy   is a mastectomy specimen with a long suture designating the lateral margin and a short suture designating the superior margin  On the specimen is a REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm skin ellipse which has a 2 5cm in diameter areola centered by a 1 3cm nipple  A vertical scar measuring 2 3cm in length  well healed  is located at the supra lateral portion of the nipple  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a biopsy cavity with an adjacent REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm firm gritty nodule is superior to the biopsy cavity  The biopsy cavity is 0 4cm from the anterior superior inked margin  The biopsy cavity measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm and is 0 3cm from the deep margin  about 3cm inferior to the biopsy cavity there is a second REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm white firm ill defined mass which is present 0 1cm from the deep margin  In addition  there is a firm 1 2cm nodule at the lateral end of the biopsy cavity  Section code  K  First nodule in relation to closest margin  L P  Biopsy cavity with adjacent second nodule  inferior nodule  in relation to deep margin  Second nodule and deep margin  Q  Third nodule  lateral  R Z  Lymph nodes Labelled  additional right axillary tissue   consists of three fragments of yellow adipose tissue aggregating REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm and is submitted entirely in cassette W  Resident  RICHARD AMMER  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  W P Andrew Lee  M D  Bruce Allan Chabner  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY PART B  BREAST  RIGHT   MASTECTOMY PART C  SOFT TISSUE  ADDITIONAL RIGHT AXILLA   EXCISION , Unchecked.
