erexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  The sections stained for estrogen and progesterone receptor proteins and HER 2 c erbB 2 do not contain invasive carcinoma  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  17 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 14 34 Consulting Pathologist s   MELINDA J  FAN  MD GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 5cm simple mastectomy specimen which is oriented by the surgeon with a short stitch designating  superior   a long stitch designating  lateral  and a double stitch designating  hot spot    intramammary node   There is a overlying REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm tan ellipse of skin with a central unremarkable 3 5cm nipple areolar complex  There is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm healed scar on the medial aspect of the nipple  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm cavity subjacent to the scar  The cavity has a smooth  hemorrhagic lining  The parenchyma surrounding the cavity is indurated with focal chalky foci  Multiple cysts are present within the tissue between the cavity and deep margin  The cavity comes to 3 0cm from the deep margin  abuts the skin  and is REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE and 17cm from the medial  superior  inferior  and lateral margins respectively  The remaining breast parenchyma is predominately fatty with delicate white fibrous tissues  The tissue adjacent to the lateral margin marked with a double stitch is ragged and hemorrhagic  No lymph nodes are identified directly at the stitch  Within the adjacent hemorrhagi