es to 0 9cm of the skin margin  A black stitch designates the axillary tail  The anterior margin is inked blue  the posterior black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm indurated tan pink nodule in the upper outer quadrant which comes to 0 4cm of the posterior margin and 0 7cm of the anterior margin  This nodule is located within a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm region of firm nodular gray pink mammary tissue which comes to 0 2cm of the posterior margin and 0 4cm of the anterior margin  Located approximately 2 5cm inferomedial and anterior to the nodule is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm cavity consistent with previous biopsy site which contains dark red blood and is surrounded by soft yellow discoloration consistent with fat necrosis  The cavity abuts the anterior margin and comes to 1 0cm of the posterior margin  The cavity is located in the mid outer breast tissue  Along the periphery of the cavity superomedially there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm indurated gray white nodular area which comes to 0 5cm of the anterior margin  The remaining cut surface displays hemorrhage and dense gray white fibrous tissue with no other discrete lesions or other gross abnormalities  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Cavity with posterior margin as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   anterior margin as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and subjacent firm nodule as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tissue between cavity and upper outer quadrant nodule   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Upper outer quadrant nodule   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Firm nodular tissue surrounding upper outer quadrant nodule submitted from medial to lateral   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tissue from upper outer quadrant which may represent lymph nodes  Received in formalin  labeled  right breast tissue mastectomy flap   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm aggregate of unre