Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  10 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  10 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 18 32 CLINICAL DATA  Positive margins on recent lumpectomy                                                                                     FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  1  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  CRIBRIFORM TYPE  EXTENSIVE  PRESENT ADJACENT TO AND AWAY FROM BIOPSY CAVITY  PRESENT IN GROSSLY UNREMARKABLE MEDIAL BREAST  PRESENT REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE DEEP MARGIN  2  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  3  INTRADUCTAL PAPILLOMAS  MULTIPLE  4  BIOPSY SITE  NOTE  There is no evidence of stromal  blood vascular or lymphatic invasion  BREAST  LEFT  INFERIOR MARGIN   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  Andrea Flieder  MD Signed On  17 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 23                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh is a left simple mastectomy specimen  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm and weighing 490 grams  Adherent to the mastectomy specimen is a portion of nipple and areola measuring REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm at its greatest dimension  On the superior aspect of the areola there is a short suture and on the inferior aspect of the areola a long suture  Also present on the mastectomy specimen is an additional small ellipse of skin measuring REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm closed with suture  This small skin ellipse is located in the lower outer quadrant  5 0cm from the inferior margin and 4 0cm from the nearest lateral resection margin  The mastectomy specimen has been sectioned at 1 0cm intervals to reveal a biopsy cavity measuring REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm  The biopsy cavity is located 1 5cm from the nearest deep surgical resection margin  0 5cm from the anterior surgical resection margin and 1 5cm from the nearest inferior surgical resection margin  In the inferior and deep portion of the biopsy cavity there is a small firm focus of tan yellow tissue  The surgical resection margins have been inked with India ink  The nipple and areolar are grossly unremarkable  Section Code  A  section of nipple and areolar  B  small ellipse of skin including recent surgical incision  lower outer quadrant   C D  inferior surgical resection margins  representative  E  lateral resection margin  representative  F  superior resection margin  representative   G H  firm yellow nodule  adjacent to biopsy cavity  and closest approximation to the deep inked surgical resection margin  I J K  sections through biopsy cavity and closest approximation to deep inked surgical resection margin  L M  section through biopsy cavity  The remainder of the breast has been sectioned at 1 0cm intervals and reveals unremarkable lobulated adipose tissue and unremarkable breast parenchyma  N  section through unremarkable breast parenchyma  medial breast   The second specimen is labeled  Left breast additional inferior margin  and consists of two fragments of breast tissue  One measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm and the other measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  The specimens have not been oriented  Upon sectioning these fragments consists of unremarkable adipose and breast parenchymal tissue  There are no foci of tumor grossly identified  This specimen has been submitted entirely in cassettes O through R  Resident  SUSAN TEBBUTT  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Michael J Yaremchuk  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY PART B  INFERIOR MARGIN  LEFT BREAST  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Radiology Outpatient Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  STEPHANIE L  SHAPIRO  M D  PHOEBE E FREER  M D  Resident  Matija Snuderl  M D  Signed Out by  Ronald Balassanian  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results Reason for Addendum  2  Additional Fluorescence In Situ Hybridization  FISH  Results CLINICAL DATA  The patient is a 30 year old woman with epidermal nevus syndrome and right bloody nipple discharge  An MRI at a referring hospital demonstrated an enhancing mass in the right breast  An ultrasound exam demonstrated 2 hypoechoic masses  Mass A is at 9 00 o clock  Mass B is at 3 00 o clock  both are 3cm from nipple  The differential diagnosis for mass A is hamartoma versus fibroadenoma  The differential diagnosis for mass B is a cyst versus fibroadenoma versus hamartoma  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  A  BREAST  RIGHT  9 00   CORE BIOPSY 1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE 2  COMPLEX SCLEROSING INTRADUCTAL PAPILLOMA  SEE NOTE  B  BREAST  RIGHT  3 00   CORE BIOPSY FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH CYST WALL  NOTE  A panel of immunohistochemical stains for cytokeratin  p63  myosin and calponin were performed on slides  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The immunostaining pattern highlights the absence of a myoepithelial layer in areas of invasive ductal carcinoma and supports the diagnosis  The results of immunohistochemical staining for estrogen receptor  progesterone receptor  and Her2 neu protein expression and of fluorescence in situ hybridization studies for Her2 neu gene amplification will be reported in an addendum  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are 2 containers which are  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received in formalin  labeled  