Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  17 AUG 95 ACCESSIONED ON  17 AUG 95 at 15 15 CLINICAL DATA  Patient status post left mastectomy for an infiltrating ductal carcinoma  Now undergoes a right breast biopsy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 1  50   AT LEAST REMOVED_DATE CM  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  CRIBRIFORM TYPE  50   SEE NOTE  NOTE  Invasion of blood vessels and lymphatic vessels is not seen  The margins of the specimen cannot be evaluated because the specimen was received in two pieces  Infiltrating and in situ carcinoma probably involve both pieces of tissue and probably extend to the margin of both pieces of tissue  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 AUG 95 at 16 51                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely 