Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  08 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  08 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 15 48 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO 1 MM OF MULTIPLE MARGINS AND LESS THAN 1 MM TO THE ANTERIOR MARGIN  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LOW GRADE  PRESENT AWAY FROM THE INVASIVE COMPONENT  NOTE  No vascular or lymphatic vessel invasion is seen  Diagnosis by  Joseph Misdraji  MD Signed On  10 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 17 01                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 40 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in frozen section lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name and unit number and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm fibroadipose tissue with orienting stitches  inked as follows  superior   black  anterior   green  posterior   yellow  inferior   blue  Sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm well demarcated firm white lobular nodule grossly abutting anterior  superior and inferior margins  Representative sections frozen as FX 1  now submitted in cassette A  Additional sections of the nodule  from lateral to medial  are in cassettes B through D  Sections from medial aspect of specimen are in cassette E  Remainder of the specimen is stored in formalin  Resident  RUBEN D  CARRASCO  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  PRESENT AT THE SUPERIOR RESECTION MARGIN  O R  Resident  JUSTIN M  CATES  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION   report_end  , Unchecked.
