Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  06 REMOVED_MONTH 99 ACCESSIONED ON  06 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 17 19 CLINICAL DATA  Invasive ductal carcinoma and ductal carcinoma in situ                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1  HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY WITH NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL CARCINOMA  2  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES AND SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  3  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 9 OF 9 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  MARYAM S  MOHAMMADKHANI  MD Signed On  10 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 17 28                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast and axillary contents   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm mastectomy with a REMOVED_DATE x 6 0cm ellipse of skin with a 4 0cm linear scar  A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm axillary tail is also identified  Inked and serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm biopsy cavity  located 0 4cm from the nearest posterior resection margin  The biopsy cavity is firm  and is surrounded by granulation tissue and fat necrosis  The surrounding breast parenchyma shows increased fibrosis with focal cystic changes  No residual tumor is identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows  biopsy cavity with the nearest posterior surgical margin in cassette A  representative sections from biopsy site in cassettes B through E  representative sections from surrounding fibrous parenchyma in cassettes F through I  Upon sectioning of axillary tail  multiple lymph nodes  ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 1 2cm are identified  The entire lymph nodes are submitted in cassettes J L  Resident  MOHAMMAD MAHMOOD  MD                                                                            