ARKABLE FAT  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Results of immunostains for cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 Cam5 2  cytokeratin 7  and pankeratin on three tissue levels support the above interpretation  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Unfixed   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVED_DATE  left breast lumpectomy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 8cm excision specimen  containing three localization wires  A long suture designates the lateral aspect  and a short suture designates the superior aspect  The long axis of the specimen runs from superior to inferior  The anterior margin of the specimen is blue  the posterior black  the medial green  and the lateral yellow  The specimen contains two separate masses  The larger spans REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm and consists of firm  tan white gritty tissue  It displays irregular borders and extends to 0 6cm from the medial margin  1 1cm from the anterior margin  3 1cm from the posterior margin  3 5cm from the lateral margin  3 3cm from the superior margin  and 1 5cm from the inferior margin  Adjacent to the mass is a hemorrhagic area containing two metal coils  The smaller mass spans REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm and consists of a tan white nodule with rounded borders  It abuts the posterior margin and extends to 0 9cm from the medial margin  2 1cm from the lateral margin  3 2cm from the anterior margin  1 8cm from the superior margin  3 5cm from the inferior margin  and 2 0cm from the larger mass  There is focal hemorrhage adjacent to the smaller mass  The remainder of the specimen consists of adipose tissue with scant fibrous tissue  Photographs are taken  The following representative sections are submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Large mass with anterior and medial margins in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and hemorrhagic site in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Hemorrhagic si